                <pb facs="1150" n="1034" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1034"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/207.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Cresson to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 21, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram October 15. Minister Price before leaving conveyed to
                    Panaman President sense of above. He regrets that Santos Railway could not be
                    included but expressed willingness to meet Department’s position. No further
                    developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cresson</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
